
## OpenAPI

```bash
ferrum-alloy openapi export --manifest ferrum-service.toml --output openapi.json
ferrum-alloy openapi export --manifest ferrum-service.toml --output openapi.json --check
```

The document is served on the management listener at `/openapi.json` (token-protected).

### AI agents

`get_item` is offered to AI agents as a read-only MCP tool. Its `#[utoipa::path]` declares `AgentTool::expose()`, and `[agents]` in `ferrum-service.toml` is enabled, so the exported document carries the `x-ferrum-mcp` extension that Ferrum Edge reads on `POST /api-specs`. Nothing else is exposed.

Expose only what an agent should be able to do on a user's behalf, and start with read-only operations. A state-changing operation needs its own `AgentTool::expose()`. The export refuses tool metadata Edge would reject or an agent could not use, such as an exposed operation without a description.
